    {
      "type": "context",
      "id": "AJ3sw",
      "x": -900,
      "y": 3860,
      "name": "Note — PieChart / Donut (Chassis)",
      "width": 420,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "PieChart / Donut — ported 2026-08-25 from Bryan's chart-chassis POC. Acceptance master for the donut variant (PRO-2755 closed; these Pencil designs are what every new chart must match, Amanda signs off).\n\nName\n• The component is PieChart, donut variant — not \"Donut Chart\". Per the 2026-08-24 naming ruling in 05-charts-theory-of-operation.md the Sc prefix is retired and ScTitledDonut becomes the PieChart donut variant. The grammar name is what engineering builds against, so the master carries it.\n\nGeometry\n• Ring 288px, inner radius 0.60 (86/144). Slices start at 12 o'clock and run clockwise.\n• The plot box is 312px, not 288 — the extra 12px on each side is room for the 8px hover explode.\n• Center total is native here: owning the arc() layer is what makes it free (theory of operation, layer 4).\n\nPalette — OPEN QUESTION for Amanda + Bryan\n• Bound to chart-sequential/seq-700 → seq-300, largest slice to smallest. Bryan's POC ramp (--chart-1..5, #0d6ad3→#9fc9f9) is monochrome blue, and that is what the sequential scale is, so this reproduces his design within a few units and inverts itself in dark mode.\n• But principle 6 says series colours come from ONE defaultChartPalette and the grammar exposes zero colour props. The other charts in this file use chart-categorical. One of the two has to be the default palette — that decision belongs upstream of this file and will move either this donut or every other chart.\n\nStates\n• Default — all series on, every slice at full strength. Also the master for the static/print path (principle 5): staticRender only strips listeners, so it is pixel-identical, and the screenshot-diff gate can compare print output against this frame.\n• Hover — focused slice explodes 8px along its centroid; the others drop to 42% opacity; tooltip and legend row-hover appear. Bryan's dim tone is the colour mixed 42% over the surface, so opacity reproduces it exactly while the fill stays a semantic token.\n• Series Off — the toggled series leaves the ring, the remaining angles and the center total recompute (95 here), and its legend row stays at 35%.\n• Missing: an Error state. AC 6 is normative and the failure block replaces the plot while the card title stays, so the donut needs its own master for that composition.\n\nAccessibility (principle 7)\n• The card header is not decoration — heading + description are what generate the SVG's aria-label. Hover data is reachable as text in both the legend and the tooltip, never colour-only.\n\nNot reproduced\n• Bryan's 9% \"hot\" lift on the focused slice. In tokens that means borrowing the next ramp step, which is the neighbouring slice's own colour. Explode plus full-vs-dim carries the emphasis instead.\n\nChassis atoms\n• Chart Legend Row — Default / Hover / Off / Focus. Hemlock's InteractiveLegend was not reused: it is a dot-marker list with no row hit-target, while Bryan's row is a 30px button with a rounded swatch, a right-aligned value and a row-hover background.\n• Chart Tooltip / Title Value — name + value(percent), the donut's two-line form.\n• Chart Error Block — the fail-loudly block (AC 6), shared by every chassis chart.\n\nSource\n• 05-charts-theory-of-operation.md · 03-chart-rendering-architecture.md · PRO-2673."
    },
